fetters.c:
#{M#Nothing can be more interesting than encountering new things. You've traveled to so many places, and I'm sure your range of experience is much broader than my own, so I was wondering if I could make a request... Have you ever encountered a flower, or spice maybe, that left a particularly strong impression on you? Could you tell me about it?
The "Inteyvat" flower... Huh, can't say I've ever heard of it, but that's certainly a grand-sounding name. Alright, well, I've made a note of it. If I'm lucky enough to ever see it in person, I'll certainly let you know.}{F#May I ask you something? The flower you wear in your hair... I've never seen one like it before. If you saw fit to fashion it into a hair accessory, I imagine it means a great deal to you.
The "Inteyvat" flower... Huh, that's certainly a grand-sounding name. I don't know how you came to possess it, but I'm sure it means you are very important to this world.}

talents.d:
When {LINK#N11250001}<color=#FFD780FF>Gravity Interference</color>{/LINK} is triggered, 4 Elemental Energy will be restored to Columbina;
Additionally, if the Lunar reaction type that accumulates the most <color=#FFD780FF>Gravity</color> for Columbina is Lunar-Charged, Lunar-Bloom, or Lunar-Crystallize, the Lunar Reaction DMG dealt by this instance of Gravity Interference is increased by 12.5%/2.5%/12.5% of Columbina's Max HP respectively. This effect can be triggered at most once every 15s.

All nearby party members' Lunar Reaction DMG is {LINK#N11190007}<color=#FFD780FF>elevated</color>{/LINK} by 1.5%.

skills.d:
The <color=#FFD780FF>{LINK#N11360002}Detection Core{/LINK}</color> created by the Elemental Skill <color=#FFD780FF>Principle: Variable Detection</color> is enhanced. Depending on the state of the <color=#FFD780FF>Detection Core</color> created:
·Steady State: All nearby party members gain 30 Elemental Mastery for each <color=#FFD780FF>{LINK#N11360001}Gradient Beacon{/LINK}</color> Mitya has;
·Overloaded: After nearby party members trigger Stellar-Conduct reactions, instead obtain 1 <color=#FFD780FF>Gradient Beacon</color> every 1.5s for 6s.
